WHAT CHANGED
  scripts/mpd-ext.mjs
    * serverNameMaxLength() parses the bound out of MPD_EXT_CONTRACT.serverNamePattern (no literal 32),
      serverNameFor(name) is the ONE helper shared by finishManifest and compareCopyToTemplate.
    * a truncating id now WARNS on stderr (new warn() helper) instead of silently shipping a different name.
    * BASE_ROLE_NAME_KEYS is built from the runtime's own roster table (mpd-roles-plugin/src/roles.data.ts,
      the module registry.ts builds its private set from) and baseRosterRoleConflicts() screens every
      derived role name with registry.roleNameKey BEFORE anything is written, refusing with
      registry.roleNameCollisionReason — the runtime's own sentence.
    * runScaffold builds in <parent>/.mpd-ext-scaffold-<pid>-<ts>/<name>, validates THAT tree, and
      renames the extension root onto the target only on success; the finally removes the container.
      The container level keeps the staged tree out of a discovery root's immediate children, so it
      is never discoverable while being built. A refusal therefore writes nothing, and the
      post-validate failure path says "refused ... nothing was written to <target>" — the old
      "this is a CLI defect" wording is gone from every refusal path.
    * --self-test: 41 -> 52 checks (new 3b long-id arm, new "plan" collision assertions).
  templates/mpd-extension/README.md + README.zh-CN.md
    * location-neutral ("the upstream template directory", "your copy"), §7 retitled --with-mcp-only,
      §6 states the template is neither discovered nor packed + the packed-tree consequence,
      §1 documents the empty-target refusal including the base-roster role collision,
      §2 states the contract-bound cap with its warning, §3 adds the roles provider/model pair rule and
      fixes the wrong "directory name must match the frontmatter name" claim.

